Comments: [Evaluator: Christian Iliadis; Date: 03/29/2024]
1.  Higher-lying, directly measured, resonances with Er > 500 keV: resonance energies are computed from Ex values from Tab. 35.15 in Endt 1990; resonance strengths
    from that table have been normalized to adopted standard strength of Elab = 1211 keV [wg = 4.37 +- 0.49 eV; see our table]; most of the strengths listed in Endt 
    1990 are given without uncertainties; in such cases, we assigned an uncertainty of 20% to the strengths.
2.  Er = 497 keV: weighted average of directly measured values by Pruissen et al. 1988 (but normalized as mentioned above) and Lovely et al. 2021.
3.  Er = 274, 411, and 473 keV: we adopted the directly measured strengths from Lovely et al. 2021; resonance energies are calculated from weighted average given in
    column 1 of Tab. III in Setoodehnia et al. 2019.
4.  Threshold resonances: contributions were estimated using Jp values from Setoodehnia et al. 2019 and Gillespie et al. 2017; C2S values were derived from
    Gillespie et al. 2017.
5.  Er = 430 keV: experimental upper limit is adopted from Lovely et al. 2021; corresponding level at Ex = 6800 keV has not been observed in (3He,d) experiment of
    Gillespie et al. 2017.
6.  Direct capture: estimated using experimental C2S values from (3He,d) experiments of Morrison 1970, Graue et al. 1969, and Gillespie et al. 2017.
